cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HAMON, please cite the paper below."
title: "HAMON — a universal, lossless harmony-label interlingua"
abstract: >-
  HAMON is an exchange layer for harmony labels across music encodings. It parses a
  harmony surface string into a typed AST, normalizes it, and round-trips it losslessly,
  keeping both the exact glyphs and the normalized meaning. hamonpy is the Python
  reference implementation.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
